# m_ix turns an array of boxes into one array: its leading axes are the
# boxes', its trailing axes the items'; an item of lower rank gets
# leading axes of length 1, a shorter one is padded at the end with its
# kind's fill (0, a space) (A9, APL2's first-axis mix).
== SOURCE
m_ix '{ r_ange _r } m_ap 1 2 3
m_ix "ab" "cde"
m_ix '{ (2 c_at _r) r_eshape 1 } m_ap 1 2
m_ix e_nclose 7 8
m_ix 1 r_eshape e_nclose 5
m_ix (e_nclose 1 2) c_at e_nclose 2 2 r_eshape 3 4 5 6
== RESULT
1 0 0
1 2 0
1 2 3
ab 
cde
1 0
1 0

1 1
1 1
7 8
5
1 2
0 0

3 4
5 6
